2024-03-08T18:38:49Z","updated_at":"2024-03-08T18:38:49Z","body":"What will be the version where we could expect this fix? Thanks","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/1986214632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/1986390557","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17914#issuecomment-1986390557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17914","id":1986390557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs52Zeod","user":{"login":"felixxm","id":2865885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjU4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2865885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-03-08T20:43:49Z","updated_at":"2024-03-08T20:43:49Z","body":"> What will be the version where we could expect this fix? Thanks\r\n\r\nDjango 5.1.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/1986390557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2214708820","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17914#issuecomment-2214708820","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17914","id":2214708820,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6EAcZU","user":{"login":"sabaimran","id":65192171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTkyMTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65192171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran","html_url":"https://github.com/sabaimran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sabaimran/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-07-08T17:00:32Z","updated_at":"2024-07-09T16:34:27Z","body":"Let me know if there's a better forum for this discussion. Happy to post elsewhere, but I thought it might be relevant to this PR.\r\n\r\nI've upgraded to `v5.1b1` locally and tried out these changes, and it still doesn't seem to be resolving this pooling issue for me. I'm using the Django ORM with a Gunicorn ASGI server + Uvicorn workers. I see that the number of my open connections to the server seems to uniformly increase. I'm testing this on PostgreSQL 15.5, arm64. Any help or consultation would be much appreciated. You can also reach me at saba at khoj.dev.\r\n\r\nThis is my configuration. I've also tried playing with `CONN_MAX_AGE`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nDATABASES = {\r\n    \"default\": {\r\n        \"ENGINE\": \"django.db.backends.postgresql\",\r\n        \"HOST\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_HOST\", \"localhost\"),\r\n        \"PORT\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_PORT\", \"5432\"),\r\n        \"USER\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_USER\", \"postgres\"),\r\n        \"NAME\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_DB\", \"khoj\"),\r\n        \"PASSWORD\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_PASSWORD\", \"postgres\"),\r\n        \"CONN_MAX_AGE\": 0,\r\n        \"CONN_HEALTH_CHECKS\": True,\r\n        },\r\n        \"OPTIONS\": {\r\n            \"default_transaction_isolation\": \"read committed\",\r\n            \"client_encoding\": \"UTF8\",\r\n            \"timezone\": \"UTC\",\r\n            \"pool\": True,\r\n        }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nOur setup is a little bespoke, so the issue could be niche. We're using FastAPI for our API layer. [See GitHub repo](https://github.com/khoj-ai/khoj).\r\n\r\n## New Info\r\n\r\nEDIT: I realized there was an error in `OPTIONS` configuration. Fixed to this:\r\n```\r\n    \"default\": {\r\n        \"ENGINE\": \"django.db.backends.postgresql\",\r\n        \"HOST\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_HOST\", \"localhost\"),\r\n        \"PORT\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_PORT\", \"5432\"),\r\n        \"USER\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_USER\", \"postgres\"),\r\n        \"NAME\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_DB\", \"khoj\"),\r\n        \"PASSWORD\": os.getenv(\"POSTGRES_PASSWORD\", \"postgres\"),\r\n        \"CONN_MAX_AGE\": 0,\r\n        \"CONN_HEALTH_CHECKS\": True,\r\n        \"OPTIONS\": {\r\n            \"pool\": True,\r\n        }\r\n    },\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich results in some connection errors, `django.db.utils.OperationalError: couldn't get a connection after 30.00 sec`. It connects at first, and the connections are stable at 4. After a few queries, the error above starts popping up. I also had to remove the other values under `OPTIONS` for the application to start up. Maybe subsequent queries aren't pulling from the pool appropriately?\r\n\r\n## Newer Info\r\n\r\nIn case anyone comes across this, our issue seems to stem from our custom setup. Because we're using FastAPI as our API layer, I think Django wasn't able to close out the DB sessions properly as each of them use different threads (`thread.local` vs `contextvars`). \r\n\r\nWe ended up using some solutions discussed in this thread: https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi/discussions/8009. This has mitigated the problem for now.\r\n\r\nNote the connection pooling within Django still doesn't work, but manually forcing all the open sessions to close from the respective threads seems to be a decent stop gap. See relevant commit here: https://github.com/khoj-ai/khoj/commit/4471c1e37fdf09d7c8bd20a9e35f29bc72b7dead.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2214708820/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2410953008","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17914#issuecomment-2410953008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17914","id":2410953008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6PtDkw","user":{"login":"Saad-Akbar-1","id":58334552,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MzM0NTUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58334552?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1","html_url":"https://github.com/Saad-Akbar-1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saad-Akbar-1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-14T11:35:35Z","updated_at":"2024-10-14T11:35:35Z","body":"@sabaimran Could explain why connection pooling still doesn't work after this PR? I'd hazard a guess that this PR should fix everything.\r\nContext: We're planning a django upgrade from 3.2 to 5.1 and we use a lot of different databases and connection pools. I'm planning the upgrade for async views support and I need to know if there would be any potential issues, so I'd be grateful for your answer here.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2410953008/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/2413374255","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/17914#issuecomment-2413374255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/17914","id":2413374255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAD-Lgs6P2Ssv","user":{"login":"pauloxnet","id":521097,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTA5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/521097?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet","html_url":"https://github.com/pauloxnet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pauloxnet/orgs"